<title>JAPAN: Capcom sells building to finance bond redemption.</title>
<headline>Capcom sells building to finance bond redemption.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Capcom Co Ltd, a maker of home computer game software, said on Wednesday it had sold one of its buildings to raise funds for the redemption of a convertible bond.</p>
<p>The company sold a three-storey building in Osaka for 4.84 billion yen to Mitsui Leasing and Development Ltd, Capcom said in a statement.</p>
<p>Mitsui Leasing is 45 percent owned by Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd.</p>
</text>
